    {
      "filename": "In The Kitchen At Sunset (47066366).jpeg",
      "title": "File:In The Kitchen At Sunset (47066366).jpeg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/83/In_The_Kitchen_At_Sunset_%2847066366%29.jpeg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:In_The_Kitchen_At_Sunset_(47066366).jpeg",
      "width": 2048,
      "height": 1365,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 3.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0",
      "artist": "Donnie Nunley",
      "description": "500px provided description: Booker T Washington National Monument had an 1863 Harvest Day celebration today. The monument celebrates the life and accomplishments of Dr. Booker T Washington, an educator, author, orator and presidential advisor. Dr. Washington was born into slavery on this farm in 1856 and remained a slave until emancipation in 1865 when he was 9 years old. \nThis lady and her partner were demonstrating and explaining the function of the kitchen on this farm during the civil war era at harvest time. It was 65 F outside and inside this small building they had built a roaring cooking fire. It was at least 95 or 100 F in the building. The change in temperature walking from the outside into the building was somewhat stunning. These ladies had 5 pots over, in and around the fire cooking dishes like chicken, cale, squash and apple pie. It smelled marvelous!\n\nA big thank you goes to this nice lady (whose name I unfortunately didn't get)  who agreed to pose by the window for me. :^) [#fire ,#hot ,#cook ,#cc ,#slavery ,#reenactor ,#1863 ,#attribution ,#Virginia ,#Kitchen ,#dbnunley ,#Booker T ,#Booker T Washington National Monument ,#Burnt Chimney ,#1863 Harvest Day ,#This place smelled absolutely delicious ,#Apple Pie in a cast iron skillet ,#chicken in vegetable casserole]",
      "dateCreated": "21 September 2013, 17:54:54 (UTC)",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "franklin-county-virginia-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "dnx4",
